 experiments 0.05 vs. quiescent cells #P","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":42.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":306.3333333333333,"r":561.6666666666666,"t":152.33333333333337},"charspan":[0,796],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/31","text":"Fig. 6. Fibrillin-1 expression in cultured cardiac fibroblasts. Quiescent cardiac fibroblasts  were stimulated for 48 h by increasing concentrations of ANG II (10 10-10-8 mol/l) (A) Or TGF-BI (10-13-10-10 mol/l) (B). SDS-soluble fibrillin-1 was analyzed by Western blot analysis (A); fibrillin-1 , collagen type I, and fibronectin deposition were measured by a in-cell-based assay (B). Data were normalized to GAPDH (A) or B-actin (B). 4 in A and n Results  are representative of 3 experiments #P 0.05 VS. quiescent cellsQuantification of myocardial fibrillin-1/S16 mRNA content by real-time RT PCR (C) is expressed fibroblasts (run in duplicate) . Quiescent cardiac fibroblasts were stimulated for 48 with ANG II (10 mol/l) Or TGF-BI (1.5 X 10-10 mol/l) . experiments 0.05 vs. quiescent cells #P"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"A","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":561.6666666666666,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":338.0,"r":346.0,"t":571.6666666666666},"charspan":[0,1],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/32","text":"A"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Fibrillin-1 (350 kDa)","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":547.6666666666666,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":478.0,"r":533.3333333333334,"t":555.6666666666666},"charspan":[0,21],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/33","text":"Fibrillin-1 (350 kDa)"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"GAPDH","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/1"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":534.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":478.3333333333333,"r":501.6666666666667,"t":540.6666666666666},"charspan":[0,5],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/34","text":"GAPDH"},{"children":[],"content_layer":